{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 857 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "a5334706a4e766bb86218407dbd1e111058a9d33b14070bad7afee08b9c76d93" :edb/db-before-t 856 :edb/db-after-t 857 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534169 50 #inst "2026-10-06T07:02:45.094Z" 13194139534169 true] [17592186124583 1020 #edb/ref 17592186280102 13194139534169 true] [17592186124583 1020 #edb/ref 17592186280126 13194139534169 true] [17592186124584 1020 #edb/ref 17592186280109 13194139534169 true] [17592186124584 1020 #edb/ref 17592186280116 13194139534169 true] [17592186124585 1020 #edb/ref 17592186280119 13194139534169 true] [17592186280102 1017 #edb/ref 17592186280103 13194139534169 true] [17592186280102 1089 "q-101316" 13194139534169 true] [17592186280102 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534169 true] [17592186280102 1100 "${lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{2{x}^{6}+7{x}^{3}-9}{2{x}^{3}-1}=$" 13194139534169 true] [17592186280102 1113 #uuid "9f201054-0384-5c36-b0e3-d164b311f9a3" 13194139534169 true] [17592186280102 1145 "First, we divide both the numerator and the denominator by the highest power of $x$ in the denominator, which is ${x}^{3}.$ Then, by noting that the reciprocals shrink to $0$ in the limit, we can then evaluate the resulting expression.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{2{x}^{6}+7{x}^{3}-9}{2{x}^{3}-1} & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{(\\frac{2{x}^{6}}{{x}^{3}}+\\frac{7{x}^{3}}{{x}^{3}}-\\frac{9}{{x}^{3}})}{(\\frac{2{x}^{3}}{{x}^{3}}-\\frac{1}{{x}^{3}})} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{(2{x}^{3}+7-\\frac{9}{{x}^{3}})}{(2-\\frac{1}{{x}^{3}})} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{2{x}^{3}+7-0}{2-0} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{lim}_{x\\to \\infty }(2{x}^{3}+7) \\\\  & =\\infty .\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534169 true] [17592186280103 1000 #edb/ref 17592186280104 13194139534169 true] [17592186280103 1000 #edb/ref 17592186280105 13194139534169 true] [17592186280103 1000 #edb/ref 17592186280106 13194139534169 true] [17592186280103 1000 #edb/ref 17592186280107 13194139534169 true] [17592186280103 1000 #edb/ref 17592186280108 13194139534169 true] [17592186280103 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534169 true] [17592186280103 1041 "selection" 13194139534169 true] [17592186280103 1104 #edb/ref 17592186280106 13194139534169 true] [17592186280103 1110 #uuid "df5d9170-f3ff-51b5-a94a-88c8d7adf1ca" 13194139534169 true] [17592186280104 1034 "\\frac{7}{2}" 13194139534169 true] [17592186280104 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534169 true] [17592186280104 1111 #uuid "fa39df28-3f8b-553a-9f48-d7f7da421b7a" 13194139534169 true] [17592186280105 1034 "9" 13194139534169 true] [17592186280105 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534169 true] [17592186280105 1111 #uuid "e888084e-700b-515d-a70b-e0794909d8a6" 13194139534169 true] [17592186280106 1034 "\\infty " 13194139534169 true] [17592186280106 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534169 true] [17592186280106 1111 #uuid "b56d6e51-8926-5292-a3ea-a06ac5508996" 13194139534169 true] [17592186280107 1034 "1" 13194139534169 true] [17592186280107 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534169 true] [17592186280107 1111 #uuid "03c22270-97f2-55a3-945e-e91a620fee86" 13194139534169 true] [17592186280108 1034 "0" 13194139534169 true] [17592186280108 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534169 true] [17592186280108 1111 #uuid "ebf77704-42ab-57a3-81c6-67ae7a0acc97" 13194139534169 true] [17592186280109 1017 #edb/ref 17592186280110 13194139534169 true] [17592186280109 1089 "q-106705" 13194139534169 true] [17592186280109 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534169 true] [17592186280109 1100 "What is the horizontal asymptote of $y=f(x)$ for $x>0$ with $f(x)=\\frac{|{x}^{3}-5|}{2-{x}^{3}}?$" 13194139534169 true] [17592186280109 1113 #uuid "0196030b-ed4f-5daa-90a4-0e2ed9bedb1e" 13194139534169 true] [17592186280109 1145 "For large positive values of $x,$ we have $|{x}^{3}-5|=({x}^{3}-5).$ Consequently, for $x\\to \\infty ,$ we get\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{|{x}^{3}-5|}{2-{x}^{3}}={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{{x}^{3}-5}{2-{x}^{3}}.\n$$\n\nThe horizontal asymptote for $x>0$ is $y={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }f(x).$ To find the horizontal asymptote, we apply the usual procedure of dividing the numerator and denominator by the highest power of $x$ in the denominator, which is ${x}^{3}.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\infty }f(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{{x}^{3}-5}{2-{x}^{3}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{(\\frac{{x}^{3}}{{x}^{3}}-\\frac{5}{{x}^{3}})}{(\\frac{2}{{x}^{3}}-\\frac{{x}^{3}}{{x}^{3}})} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{(1-\\frac{5}{{x}^{3}})}{(\\frac{2}{{x}^{3}}-1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{1-0}{0-1} \\\\  & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the horizontal asymptote is $y=-1.$" 13194139534169 true] [17592186280110 1000 #edb/ref 17592186280111 13194139534169 true] [17592186280110 1000 #edb/ref 17592186280112 13194139534169 true] [17592186280110 1000 #edb/ref 17592186280113 13194139534169 true] [17592186280110 1000 #edb/ref 17592186280114 13194139534169 true] [17592186280110 1000 #edb/ref 17592186280115 13194139534169 true] [17592186280110 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534169 true] [17592186280110 1041 "selection" 13194139534169 true] [17592186280110 1104 #edb/ref 17592186280111 13194139534169 true] [17592186280110 1110 #uuid "bb1d649c-c5ca-508b-a63d-05953e6a21b1" 13194139534169 true] [17592186280111 1034 "y=-1" 13194139534169 true] [17592186280111 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534169 true] [17592186280111 1111 #uuid "4aed695e-67c1-5dcd-96ff-6b41b1965a30" 13194139534169 true] [17592186280112 1034 "y=-3" 13194139534169 true] [17592186280112 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534169 true] [17592186280112 1111 #uuid "72e2d26f-bee9-58f1-92e7-547d7039c083" 13194139534169 true] [17592186280113 1034 "No horizontal asymptote" 13194139534169 true] [17592186280113 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534169 true] [17592186280113 1111 #uuid "2346d9fb-ee46-5705-924b-38fdf3d6a505" 13194139534169 true] [17592186280114 1034 "y=2" 13194139534169 true] [17592186280114 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534169 true] [17592186280114 1111 #uuid "85335e6f-22ab-530e-8b8f-cd732d8e43ea" 13194139534169 true] [17592186280115 1034 "y=1" 13194139534169 true] [17592186280115 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534169 true] [17592186280115 1111 #uuid "b55e61f3-5da5-5388-8d15-1210bb4ff4ef" 13194139534169 true] [17592186280116 1017 #edb/ref 17592186280117 13194139534169 true] [17592186280116 1089 "q-302240" 13194139534169 true] [17592186280116 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534169 true] [17592186280116 1100 "What is the horizontal asymptote of $y=f(x)$ for $x<0$ with $f(x)=\\frac{|8x-7|}{-5x+2}?$\n\nThe horizontal asymptote is $y=$\n\n{{field-1}}." 13194139534169 true] [17592186280116 1113 #uuid "143183aa-b87e-56d7-a491-9ddede7028da" 13194139534169 true] [17592186280116 1145 "For large negative values of $x,$ we have $|8x-7|=-(8x-7).$ Consequently, for $x\\to -\\infty ,$ we get\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }\\frac{|8x-7|}{-5x+2}={lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }\\frac{-(8x-7)}{-5x+2}.\n$$\n\nThe horizontal asymptote for $x<0$ is $y={lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }f(x).$ To find the horizontal asymptote, we apply the usual procedure of dividing the numerator and denominator by the highest power of $x$ in the denominator, which is $x.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }f(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }\\frac{-(8x-7)}{-5x+2} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }\\frac{-(\\frac{8x}{x}-\\frac{7}{x})}{(\\frac{-5x}{x}+\\frac{2}{x})} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }\\frac{-(8-\\frac{7}{x})}{(-5+\\frac{2}{x})} \\\\  & =\\frac{-(8-0)}{-5+0} \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the horizontal asymptote is $y=\\frac{8}{5}.$" 13194139534169 true] [17592186280117 1000 #edb/ref 17592186280118 13194139534169 true] [17592186280117 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534169 true] [17592186280117 1041 "field-1" 13194139534169 true] [17592186280117 1104 #edb/ref 17592186280118 13194139534169 true] [17592186280117 1110 #uuid "347827f2-cb32-5655-9539-044dcf23f8a2" 13194139534169 true] [17592186280118 1034 "\\frac{8}{5}" 13194139534169 true] [17592186280118 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534169 true] [17592186280118 1111 #uuid "d66a3589-0da5-5f32-ba48-a506c649a6ff" 13194139534169 true] [17592186280119 1017 #edb/ref 17592186280120 13194139534169 true] [17592186280119 1089 "q-35835" 13194139534169 true] [17592186280119 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534169 true] [17592186280119 1100 "Find the horizontal asymptote of the function $f(x)=\\frac{-5{x}^{7}+1}{10{x}^{3}+x+3}.$" 13194139534169 true] [17592186280119 1113 #uuid "7e620762-9516-52ae-860d-cc352b75f611" 13194139534169 true] [17592186280119 1145 "The horizontal asymptote is $y={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }f(x).$ To find the horizontal asymptote, we apply the usual procedure of dividing the numerator and denominator by the highest power of $x$ in the denominator, which is ${x}^{3}.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\infty }f(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{-5{x}^{7}+1}{10{x}^{3}+x+3} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{(-\\frac{5{x}^{7}}{{x}^{3}}+\\frac{1}{{x}^{3}})}{(\\frac{10{x}^{3}}{{x}^{3}}+\\frac{x}{{x}^{3}}+\\frac{3}{{x}^{3}})} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{(-5{x}^{4}+\\frac{1}{{x}^{3}})}{(10+\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}+\\frac{3}{{x}^{3}})} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{-5{x}^{4}+0}{10+0+0} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}{lim}_{x\\to \\infty }{x}^{4} \\\\  & =-\\infty .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThe limit does not come out to a finite number. Therefore, there is no horizontal asymptote." 13194139534169 true] [17592186280120 1000 #edb/ref 17592186280121 13194139534169 true] [17592186280120 1000 #edb/ref 17592186280122 13194139534169 true] [17592186280120 1000 #edb/ref 17592186280123 13194139534169 true] [17592186280120 1000 #edb/ref 17592186280124 13194139534169 true] [17592186280120 1000 #edb/ref 17592186280125 13194139534169 true] [17592186280120 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534169 true] [17592186280120 1041 "selecti